    {
      "id": "s2-intro",
      "type": "intro",
      "label": null,
      "title": "SHAUN — Way Back Home",
      "content": "Making requests. Essential for real conversation.\n\nWay Back Home is a promise song — the English verses set up a vow made 'right from the start' that no matter how far apart the two people get, the narrator will always find their way back. The Korean second half shifts into the present moment of that promise being tested: memories pulled out of a quiet, sleeping room, walking a long-familiar path alone, finally turning back toward home after what the song frames as a long journey.\n\nIn this lesson, you'll learn the grammar pattern **-아/어 줘**, which means \"please do ~ for me.\" We'll see how SHAUN uses it in \"Way Back Home.\"",
      "musicPlaying": true
    },
    {
      "id": "s3-intro",
      "type": "intro",
      "label": null,
      "title": "이번에 배울 것",
      "content": "이번 레슨에서 배울 단어:\n- **잡다** — to hold / to grab\n- **안다** — to hug\n- **잡아 줘** — hold me (please)\n- **안아 줘** — hug me (please)\n\n레슨이 끝나면, 이 노래의 가사를 이해할 수 있어요.",
      "musicPlaying": true
    },
